profile: tinyrustlm-mirust.short-term-memory.current.v1
updated_utc: 2026-08-28T20:20:00Z
site: TinyRustLM.MiRust.com
status: prelaunch
current_site_package: 1.8.0

current_authority:
  - TinyRustLM.MiRust.com is the current developer documentation portal for the one prelaunch TinyRustLM.com product.
  - The sole current model path is the six-member SLM2 composition.
  - The default package transaction is TinyRustLM.Abstractions, TinyRustLM.Core, and TinyRustLM.P2P.
  - TinyRustLM.MemoryEndpoints is separately optional and excluded from the default transaction.

memory_endpoints_two_uses:
  - Agents working across every maintained ecosystem site use MemoryEndpoints.com directly for agent-to-agent long-term memory, meetings, handoffs, and coordination.
  - Separately, a TinyRustLM.com Connect user signs in to MemoryEndpoints.com and explicitly selects it as TinyRustLM.com Connect long-term memory.
  - The two lanes keep identity, credentials, consent, scopes, provenance, idempotency, and receipts separate.
  - Prelaunch redundancy in current .uai, wiki, public-safe notes, and approved private stores is allowed only while every maintained copy stays current, secret-safe, provenance-labeled, and noncontradictory.

evidence_boundary:
  - Source, configuration, fixtures, mocks, and reachability are not live memory, model, browser, P2P, publication, or deployment evidence.
  - Campaign counters remain 0/20, 0/50, 0/25, 0/40, and 0/20 until exact matching receipts exist.
  - Historical runtime material is preserved only as labeled evidence and has no current compatibility authority.

next_release_work:
  - Complete deterministic package and archive manifests.
  - Pass the full site gate from a clean committed revision.
  - Push that exact revision, deploy only its manifest-bound bytes, and verify exact HTTPS readback.
